      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear that, but \"fleeting moments\" don't really feel like enough when the decay is so absolute. it's like trying to hold water in a sieve. if the end result is always going to be zero, and everything i do just accelerates the exhaustion of my own resources... it starts to feel like the only logical response to a system that's broken is to stop participating in it. to just accept the equilibrium. is there actually any dignity in fighting something that's mathematically destined to win?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
